    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūtrībĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		nutrio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>nourishing, nutritious</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 5, 1, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nutribiliores suci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 10, 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Acut. 2, 37, 212</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūtrī-bĭlia</span></b> ,
				ium, n., <i>nourishing
				food</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Tard. 1, 4,
			108</span></i>.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nūtrībĭlĭ-ter</span></b> ,
				<i>so as to be nourished</i> or <i>reared</i>, <i><span class="en">Theod. Prisc. 4, 2</span></i>.
				</div>
